{
  "_doc": "Apps auth-parity.mjs probes every day: each app with a sign-in page, its live origin and the paths of its sign-in, sign-up and recovery pages. `runtime` says which server probes apply: accountkit (better-auth endpoints answer), compat (AccountKit behind its Auth.js bridge; Auth.js-shaped endpoints answer), authjs (Auth.js), gotrue (Supabase GoTrue), legacy (the product's own). The inventory behind this list is docs/auth-parity-2026-11-01.md. Adding an app with a sign-in page is one row here. `providerButtons: \"OC\"` marks an app whose Google/GitHub buttons are OrangeCat with a provider hint (Skif), so they count as OC, not as Morulia. `standard: true` marks an app on AccountKit's own screens (`screens: \"accountkit\"` or its runtime directly): every method but MOR must be on, Lightning login (LN) included, in AccountKit's order, with AccountKit's words on the links between sign-in and sign-up. `ownProviders` names providers an app signs in with through its own registered app (Loki's GitHub, AccountKit `githubSignIn`); a button naming only those is not Morulia's. `served: false` lists an app with accounts that is not served yet; it is reported, not probed.",
  "apps": [
